      "content": "thanks for explaining that. but i'm still stuck on the \"technically possible\" part. you mentioned it's unlikely due to dispersion and regulations, but what if they didn't use high concentrations? \n\nlike, if they used something extremely potent but at a sub-threshold level where you wouldn't even smell it as a \"scent,\" but your body still reacts chemically? wouldn't something like an olfactory-targeted neurotransmitter modulator work even in tiny amounts? i feel like if there's even a theoretical way for a compound to cross the blood-brain barrier through inhalation, the \"impossibility\" part is just a matter of how much money they're willing to spend on the tech.",
      "source": "evaluator"
